{"availability":"available","full":"xcontcom/perfect-shuffle-cryptography","name":"perfect-shuffle-cryptography","description":"This project demonstrates a minimalist, fully deterministic file encryption scheme built from perfect shuffle permutations","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":82,"forks":1,"created":"2025-07-02T23:18:25Z","updated":"2025-07-07T13:56:22Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["cryptography","cryptography-algorithms","cryptography-tools","javascript","nodejs","obfuscation","perfect-shuffle"],"demo":"https://xcontcom.github.io/perfect-shuffle-cryptography/shuffle_png_web/shuffle_png_web_modes.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.903Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.903Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.903Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.903Z","stars":82,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Welcome to Perfect Shuffle Cryptography, a lightweight and elegant encryption tool that uses a deterministic perfect shuffle algorithm to secure data. Featuring the spirit of Reefer, the chonky cat, this project provides two implementations: a file-based encryption tool (shufflefile.js) for securing files like images, and a text-based demo (shuffletext.html) for interactive exploration. Whether you're David sending encrypted cat pics to Jimmy or just curious about permutation-based cryptography, this project has you covered!","A perfect shuffle is a permutation technique where a sequence (like a deck of cards or a string of bits) is split into two equal halves and interleaved in a specific order. This project uses two types of perfect shuffles to encrypt and decrypt data:","The sequence of in-shuffles (represented by 1) and out-shuffles (represented by 0) is determined by a binary key. For example, a key of 101 means: in-shuffle, out-shuffle, in-shuffle. This deterministic shuffling obscures the data, making it secure without the key."],"features":["In-Shuffle: The second half of the sequence is interleaved with the first half, starting with the second half. For a sequence [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8] (split into [1, 2, 3, 4] and [5, 6, 7, 8]), an in-shuffle produces…","Out-Shuffle: The first half of the sequence is interleaved with the second half, starting with the first half. For [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], an out-shuffle produces [1, 5, 2, 6, 3, 7, 4, 8]."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/xcontcom/perfect-shuffle-cryptography/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7fb75ad7443678d6804456ebcd98ff0185246a232fc6a317f3047f25b6f03098","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.990Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.990Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Welcome to Perfect Shuffle Cryptography, a lightweight and elegant encryption tool that uses a deterministic perfect shuffle algorithm to secure data. Featuring the spirit of Reefer, the chonky cat, this project provides two implementations: a file-based encryption tool (shufflefile.js) for securing files like images, and a text-based demo (shuffletext.html) for interactive exploration. Whether you're David sending encrypted cat pics to Jimmy or just curious about permutation-based cryptography, this project has you covered!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/xcontcom/perfect-shuffle-cryptography/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7fb75ad7443678d6804456ebcd98ff0185246a232fc6a317f3047f25b6f03098","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/xcontcom/perfect-shuffle-cryptography/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.991Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-07-07T13:56:22Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/xcontcom/perfect-shuffle-cryptography/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.992Z","hash":"7fb75ad7443678d6804456ebcd98ff0185246a232fc6a317f3047f25b6f03098","originalBytes":9023,"storedBytes":9023,"truncated":fal